            </h2>

            <p>
                In Lesson 8, we introduced GitHub Copilot as an AI coding
                assistant.
            </p>

            <p>
                In this lesson, we will focus more closely on how Copilot
                becomes part of a developer's working environment,
                how developers access it, why account authentication is
                required, and why subscription limits should be understood
                before depending heavily on AI coding tools.
            </p>

            <p>
                We will use Visual Studio Code as our main example because
                it provides a common environment for learning AI-assisted
                software development.
            </p>

        </section>

