        <section id="practical">

            <h2>
                Practical Setup Example
            </h2>

            <p>
                A beginner developer can think of Copilot setup as this
                workflow:
            </p>

            <ol>
                <li>
                    Install or open Visual Studio Code.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Locate GitHub Copilot in the editor.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Sign in with the correct GitHub account.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Confirm your available Copilot access.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Open a code project.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Start with a small coding task.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Review every suggestion before accepting it.
                </li>
            </ol>

            <h3>
                Example Prompt
            </h3>

            <pre><code>Create a simple HTML heading
for Elmi Guray Academy.</code></pre>

            <h3>
                Possible Result
            </h3>

            <pre><code>&lt;h1&gt;
    Elmi Guray Academy
&lt;/h1&gt;</code></pre>

            <h3>
                Browser Output
            </h3>

            <h1>
                Elmi Guray Academy
            </h1>

        </section>

